'' 'union' used to require a name, so an anonymous one reported TKO0406 and lost every
'' member of the enclosing type. Anonymity is legal only INSIDE another aggregate --
'' a bare 'type' at module level is still an error, which is why the parser tracks
'' how many aggregate bodies enclose the cursor rather than accepting both.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-symbols tests/parser/src/anon-union.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-MAX-DIAG: 0
'' The count is the assertion: all FOUR fields -- b0, b1 from the anonymous inner
'' type, w from the anonymous union, and tail -- land in T's own scope. Merely
'' appearing somewhere in the dump would also be true if each opened its own scope,
'' which is exactly the wrong answer.
'' EXPECT-OUT: scope 3 type of 't' parent=2 (4)
'' EXPECT-OUT: field     'tail'
